// The faces Undermere's things wear until they are known: each run deals them out
// afresh from its seed, one to a kind, so a murky potion is healing in one run and
// fire in the next. A thing of an unknown kind is called by its face and drawn in its
// colour, and keeps that colour once its kind is known, so the colour never gives a
// kind away. What each thing is and does is `items.ron`; this is only how it looks.
//
// Every field (the ones marked "optional" may be left out):
//   tag:     a tag from `items.ron`, "potion" | "scroll" | "staff" | "wand" | "ring"; every
//            kind carrying it wears one of this family's faces, and no kind may carry the
//            tags of two families
//   called:  what a thing of an unknown kind is called, with {} where its face goes:
//            "{} potion" makes "murky potion", which the log says as "a murky potion"
//   faces:   optional; [(name:, color:)] the faces dealt out, at least one for each kind
//            the family has; name is the word, color (r, g, b) in 0..=1 what a thing
//            wearing it is drawn in
//   titles:  optional; (syllables:, words:, length:, color:) titles made up instead, one
//            to a kind and no two alike: words of syllables in upper case, (fewest, most)
//            words to a title and (fewest, most) syllables to a word, each one at least,
//            and the colour every thing with a title is drawn in
//
// A family has faces or titles, and not both.
[
    (
        tag: "potion",
        called: "{} potion",
        faces: [
            (name: "murky", color: (0.55, 0.47, 0.32)),
            (name: "crimson", color: (0.9, 0.16, 0.24)),
            (name: "violet", color: (0.62, 0.36, 0.9)),
